# LinkedIn Posts — Lily Ray

## Post 1

**Date:** January 20, 2026

**Topic:** Reflection on SEO, GEO & AI Search in 2025 — separating signal from noise

**Summary:**
Lily Ray published a year-in-review piece arguing that 2025 was defined by a naming frenzy (GEO, AEO, LLMO) driven largely by newcomers with tools to sell, and that most advice being shared was either rebranded SEO or actively dangerous. Her core observation: every article she published in 2025 — regardless of platform — was cited in LLMs within hours, without doing anything specifically for GEO, simply because LLMs rely on search engines and the content ranked well. She warned that AI-generated content at scale, self-promotional tactics, and vibe-coded tracking tools flooding inboxes were creating a wave of low-quality manipulation that would eventually be corrected.

**Source:** https://lilyraynyc.substack.com/p/a-reflection-on-seo-and-ai-search
**Referenced via LinkedIn:** https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lily-ray-44755615_a-reflection-on-seo-geo-ai-search-in-2025-activity-7419213086412251136-etQU

**Relevance to research:**
Establishes Ray's foundational 2026 position: strong traditional SEO performance is the actual mechanism behind AI search visibility, and most GEO-specific tactics are either unnecessary or risky. Useful as a baseline against which her later, more specific warnings can be read.

