## Post 2

**Date:** March 18, 2026

**Topic:** GEO tactics that actively destroy SEO performance

**Summary:**
Ray published a detailed Substack piece — shared widely on LinkedIn — arguing that popular GEO tactics are structurally self-defeating because AI search retrieval is built on RAG (Retrieval Augmented Generation), meaning content must be indexed and ranking in search engines to even enter an LLM's context window. She cited multiple independent studies confirming ChatGPT relies heavily on Google's index for retrieval, including via SerpAPI. Her specific targets: scaled AI-generated content, self-promotional listicles, and "Mount AI" — Glenn Gabe's term for the rapid spike-and-crash pattern she sees repeatedly across sites using these tactics. She documented one company that published 2,000 self-promotional articles and saw simultaneous drops in both organic traffic and ChatGPT citations in late January 2026.

**Source:** https://lilyraynyc.substack.com/p/your-geo-strategy-might-be-destroying
**Referenced via LinkedIn:** multiple shares and commentary threads

**Relevance to research:**
The most technically grounded piece in her 2026 output. Directly connects RAG architecture to why SEO and GEO cannot be decoupled — and why tactics that harm SEO will, by definition, harm AI search visibility. Strongest evidence base for the argument that there is no shortcut path to LLM citation.

