## Post 3

**Date:** May 6, 2026

**Topic:** Google search results shifting toward authentic first-person content and forums

**Summary:**
Ray published a LinkedIn post observing that Google's results have visibly evolved to favor authentic first-person content and forum discussions over generic optimized pages — a pattern she sees as consistent with Google's long-running effort to surface real human voices over SEO-first content.

**Source:** LinkedIn post, covered by PPC Land
**Reference:** https://ppc.land/lily-ray-what-the-seo-industry-is-getting-dangerously-wrong-about-ai-search/

**Relevance to research:**
Short but significant signal — reinforces the E-E-A-T and real-human-content thread running through all of Ray's 2026 commentary. Aligns with Aleyda Solis's parallel point about user-generated content and forum mentions gaining weight in AI citation.

